Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.540 align:start position:0%
 
you  Macerich master is a new game from MMO  publisher and see soft it features  elements of both a classic MOBA game and  a dungeon crawler I recently got  hands-on with the MXM alpha and got to  experience both these avenues of  gameplay when I look back on my hands on  time with game the first thing that  comes to mind is the large amount of  content on offer from the very start the  player versus player aspect of the game  will be familiar to anyone who's played  any MOBA game but with one major change  you get to pick two characters instead  of just one and exam sets itself apart  from other games in the genre by  offering players the option to instantly  tag out to another master players choose  two masters at the beginning of each PvP  match and knowing when to tag out adds  another layer of strategy tagging can be  used to dodge certain moves or even  avoid death when a master is tagged out  they'll slowly regenerate health fault  benched  combat moves pretty fast and I found a  lot of it to rely on skill shots and  twitch reflexes movement plays a big  part I chose the control scheme which  moved my character around using WASD and  hitting spacebar to jump some maps have  verticality with obstacles to jump over  and platforms to leap onto and timing  dashes using right click was super  important for dodging attacks it's easy  to jump into the arena for a match that  goes for about 5 minutes you once the  timer ends the team with the most kills  wins the game also offers matches  against AI so that players can ease  themselves into the game play at their  own pace at the beginning of each match  a master selection screen is presented  which allows players to choose the  characters that they want to play and  equip skins skills or stat boosting  nodes I was quite surprised how similar  the screen looks compared to the League  of Legends champion selection screen  right down to the skin selection submenu  outside of pvp arena matches MXN offers  dungeon crawler style content as well  dungeons are short enough that they  don't quite feel like a grind and boss  fights have enough action to bring each  area to a satisfying clues the story  missions introduced each feature of  gameplay gradually and although I  thought there was a lot to do the  tutorial missions were great in helping  me gradually understand the game's many  systems some of these segments were  peppered with some cheesy cutscenes to  break up the tedium but fortunately  everything was skippable completing  these missions and me rewards which I  could use to unlock new masters in their  skins and there were a lot of different  options on offer among these were  characters from some of ncsoft other  popular MMO games including Guild Wars 2  wildstar ion and linear to there are a  fair amount of options available for  changing up a masters appearance  skillset and stats stats are changeable  by equipping nodes and players can mix  and match nodes to go for more offensive  defensive or supportive builds according  to their preference overall I can see  potential for a lot of strategic depth  when approaching in maxim's PvP arena  and when that becomes a little too full  on there's always the dungeon crawling  aspect to fall back on to as well my  time with the Alpha was a fun mix of  fast-paced competitive play and  satisfying monster killing and it's  piqued my interest enough for me to be  curious about what the full game has to  offer when it's finally out  you

